    {
      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "T1H1N5C7",
        "Description": "NAND reading (inputs A and B, BIAS constantly on, threshold 0.125) of the shipped \u0027Logic Gate NOT-NAND\u0027 gate. Role in the 4-bit adder: carry-OR copy 7 of stage 1: Y = NAND(A1, B1), feeding T1H1CARRYC7.A. The whole 4-bit adder composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate\u0027s truth table is extracted once in isolation, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction \u2014 there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here. The fan-out of the A, B and Cin bits onto several gates happens at the logic layer (each gate input is driven by the same network bit); shared stages \u2014 and each stage\u0027s carry-out, which must reach the next stage\u0027s several carry-in pins \u2014 are duplicated as extra gate instances because the canvas wires one waveguide per pin (like NAND1A/NAND1B in \u0027Logic Gate Half Adder\u0027).",
        "Identifier": "group_cf99020b1a9f4d4f94880e1df2f5d7dd",
        "IdGuid": "85423e74-dc1b-42e0-9763-cb215793d922",
        "ChildComponentGuids": [
          "85f95175-c04c-4c3e-bb14-25f2c4d15537",
          "885f3019-c422-4cd9-afad-5b2d2c6fa6cf",
          "1bb7c95d-9b62-4c90-9352-a9df306712df",
